# Understanding DTO (Data Transfer Object) Pattern

## What is DTO?
- Design pattern for data transfer between client and server
- Helps optimize network communication
- Separates data transfer objects from domain entities
- Allows customized data structures for specific needs

## DTO Flow Diagram
```
Client <----DTO----> Server
   │                    │
   └─── HTTP Request ───┘
   └─── HTTP Response ──┘
```

## Key Benefits

### 1. Reduced Network Calls
Example Scenario:
```java
// Without DTO (3 separate API calls)
Organization org = getOrganization();     // API call 1
List<Department> deps = getDepartments(); // API call 2
List<Employee> emps = getEmployees();     // API call 3

// With DTO (single API call)
OrganizationDTO dto = getOrganizationDetails(); // Contains all data
```

### 2. Data Encapsulation
```java
// Entity (Internal)
public class User {
    private Long id;
    private String firstName;
    private String lastName;
    private String email;
    private String password;    // Sensitive
    private String secretKey;   // Sensitive
    private Date createdAt;     // Internal
}

// DTO (External)
public class UserDTO {
    private Long id;
    private String firstName;
    private String lastName;
    private String email;
    // Excludes sensitive/internal data
}
```

## Real-World Example

### Entity Hierarchy
```java
